// Every binding in this language writes its type: `int x = 5;`, `case
// Circle(int r):`, `for (int x in xs)`, every parameter, every field. An
// inferred lambda parameter would be the first name introduced without one,
// and it would need the interface's types pushed INTO the body -- a second
// direction of inference in a language that has only ever had the outward
// one. Relaxing this later is additive, which is why the restrictive choice
// is the reversible one.
interface Get { int of(int a); }
Get g = (a) => a;
print(g.of(1));
